{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_event_dispatcher_eventdispatcher", "label": "eventDispatcher builder", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A typed builder whose Handled type parameter tracks which event kinds have handlers, so build only type-checks once every variant is covered.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/event-dispatcher.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_event_dispatcher_compile_time_exhaustiveness", "label": "Compile-time exhaustiveness", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "ts-pattern exhaustive and assertNever both check at runtime or rely on the author remembering; the builder moves the check to compile time, and the error names the missing kind so the fix is mechanical.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/event-dispatcher.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_event_dispatcher_eventdispatcherincomplete", "label": "EventDispatcherIncomplete marker", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "build returns a non-callable value when kinds remain, and an __unhandled phantom field carries the missing kind so the type error is informative.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/event-dispatcher.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_event_dispatcher_switch_fallthrough_hazard", "label": "A plain switch silently swallows new kinds", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "An unhandled kind falls through to return state, so adding a variant makes replay produce wrong state with nothing failing - the event just never contributes.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/event-dispatcher.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_